  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health Development Program (HDP) is a nationwide TB-organisation with over 31 000 volunteers in 1 100 localities covering all 18 states. The project empowers and support community systems that deliver integrated people centered, gender- focused care through mobile clinics, screening, contact tracing, treatment support, food support and capacity building of volunteers and health workers. In the current context of war the work towards IDPs, refugees and women exposed to violence, has been intensified.</narrative>
  </description>
